I like most of the patch except for this.  The reason is not balance. 
I think this is quite balanced.  I don't think it is consistent with
the rest of the Nethack universe.

Nethack gods are not omnipotent.  There are plenty of times when they
would like to just kill you, but they can't.  The best they can do is
throw some minions or powerful magic at you.

The best example is if you really piss off Moloch.  He hits you with a
wide-angle disintegration beam, which destroys your armor, and you if
you're not resistant.  Pretty darn powerful, but you can survive it. 
And if you do, Moloch is left frustrated.  If gods could take your
items, wouldn't Moloch want to do so as soon as he became aware of
you?  Especially, say, the AoY?

Other times, gods will try to blast you with elements (like if you
attack a priest in a temple).  If gods were capable of taking items
from you, wouldn't they do so?  Especially an item granting you
resistance to their spells?

So from these, I conclude that Nethack gods do not have the power to
take items from you.

I've always had the feeling that in this case Nethack follows D&D.  A
human that becomes powerful enough could smack a god around.  And
irreverent as I am, I've always taken great pleasure in that
possibility.  Maybe that's why I object to beefing the gods like this.

